agic backstory  that had led to the army doctor's  imprisonment in broadmoor  murray and minor shared letters for some  time but murray was always careful to  keep what he knew of miner's situation  to himself when the men did eventually  meet it was the start of a genuine  friendship that lasted many years and  included murray making numerous visits  to broadmoor  some have speculated that william  miner's work on the dictionary was  useful therapy for him  but by 1902 his grip on reality was all  but gone  he believed that every night he was  abducted and taken to various locations  where he was forced to do unspeakable  things  a delusion that eventually led to him  cutting off his own penis  murray as well as other family and  friends campaigned to have minor  repatriated and finally in 1910 he was  released from broadmoor and sent back to  america where he spent the remaining  years of his life at saint elizabeth's  hospital  william miner was a tortured soul  but a keenly intelligent man who made an  extraordinary contribution to the  english language  next time you don't understand the word  it may be thanks to one of his 10 000  contributions to the oxford english  dictionary that you end up a little  wiser in linguistic terms he's an unsung  hero and for that he deserves our  gratitude  or appreciation  or regard  thanks for watching

